title: Walk_GregoryOfNyssa_Augustine
tags: walk
speaker: Gregory
---
Gregory: We have explored what exists and the nature of created reality.
Gregory: Now you seek to understand how the human mind grasps that reality.
Gregory: Our path leads from the Metaphysics grove across to Epistemology.
Gregory: Tall pines line this winding trail in the clear forest light.
Gregory: To know what is real, we must examine how we gain true knowledge.
Gregory: Bishop Augustine waits in the shaded grove ahead.
Gregory: He pondered how divine light illuminates the human intellect to perceive truth.
Gregory: He will question how your mind separates solid knowledge from deceptive error.
Gregory: Consider whether truth is discovered within the soul or received from without.
Gregory: Let us enter his clearing and join his inquiry into knowledge.
===
